WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.862
Validation is still required in Spark.

00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:08.852
A distributed pipeline that finishes successfully can still produce the wrong result.

00:00:08.852 --> 00:00:11.397
State the expected row grain.

00:00:11.397 --> 00:00:14.347
Compare totals when the measure is additive.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:17.397
Check row counts at important stages.

00:00:17.397 --> 00:00:23.637
Inspect unexpected null values. Confirm that joins did not multiply the data.

00:00:23.637 --> 00:00:28.408
And review the execution plan for unnecessarily large scans or shuffles.

00:00:28.992 --> 00:00:31.719
Think of validation as having two sides.

00:00:31.719 --> 00:00:35.499
First, is the result analytically correct?

00:00:35.499 --> 00:00:41.014
Second, is the pipeline doing the work in a reasonable way for the scale of the data?

00:00:41.014 --> 00:00:45.271
A trustworthy pipeline should be both correct and explainable.
